ations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4-10t \\\\ y=-1+6t \\\\ z=7-7t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387789 13194139536186 true] [17592186387788 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387790 13194139536186 true] [17592186387788 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536186 true] [17592186387788 1041 "field-1" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387788 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387790 13194139536186 true] [17592186387788 1110 #uuid "972fddde-e04a-509f-9690-14e4c1781376" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387789 1034 "4+10t" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387789 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536186 true] [17592186387789 1111 #uuid "3c0d844e-3002-5654-b452-82e82c9ecb5e" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387790 1034 "4-10t" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387790 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536186 true] [17592186387790 1111 #uuid "df6efcda-6ade-5b9d-b2d7-67cd9ddad7dc" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387791 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387792 13194139536186 true] [17592186387791 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536186 true] [17592186387791 1041 "field-2" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387791 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387792 13194139536186 true] [17592186387791 1110 #uuid "12c170be-d58b-5b9a-acf1-3ceb5eaa1bfb" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387792 1034 "1" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387792 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536186 true] [17592186387792 1111 #uuid "fb8aabd0-2293-59ac-8349-165ae059e857" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387793 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387794 13194139536186 true] [17592186387793 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536186 true] [17592186387793 1041 "field-3" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387793 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387794 13194139536186 true] [17592186387793 1110 #uuid "fe848625-8986-51f5-8b38-a149e58da0bb" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387794 1034 "-1+6t" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387794 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536186 true] [17592186387794 1111 #uuid "544a794c-a04f-5e71-a860-dca80039ddf0" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387796 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387798 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1089 "q-236992" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1100 "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(4,1,-1)$ and $Q(6,5,1).$\n\n| $x=$ | $4+2t$ | $t\\in [0,$ {{field-1}} $]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $1+4t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | {{field-2}} |  |" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1113 #uuid "f1169269-03fd-50a6-b745-72b26940d1b6" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387795 1145 "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ 4t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4+2t \\\\ 1+4t \\\\ -1+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\i