7800 1145 "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,3,2)$ and $Q(2,4,5).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3t \\\\ 3+t \\\\ 2+3t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+3t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=2+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387802 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387803 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387804 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387805 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387806 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1041 "selection" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387803 13194139536186 true] [17592186387801 1110 #uuid "e4ee4ccc-fa21-55ed-bbc2-6465ec027521" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387802 1034 "{\\begin{aligned}x=2-t \\\\ y=4+3t \\\\ z=5+2t\\end{aligned}" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387802 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536186 true] [17592186387802 1111 #uuid "233e8511-39eb-5fe4-bd69-b751703ab2a1" 13194139536186 t