 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387819 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536186 true] [17592186387819 1111 #uuid "2c764bd5-a90e-5d79-aa15-b24d7a4ae25b" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387820 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387821 13194139536186 true] [17592186387820 1089 "q-70716" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387820 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536186 true] [17592186387820 1100 "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+1 \\\\ y=3-t \\\\ z=t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." 13194139536186 true] [17592186387820 1113 #uuid "b1a4efcc-8584-528a-9f17-a5e1e08f2760" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387820 1145 "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2t+1 \\\\ 3-t \\\\ t+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,3,2)$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139536186 true] [17592186387821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387822 13194139536186 true] [17592186387821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387823 13194139536186 true] [17592186387821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387824 13194139536186 true] [17592186387821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387825 13194139536186 true] [17592186387821 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387826 13194139536186 true] [17592186387821 1040 #edb/